{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.GramWeightedQvalue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.GramWeightedQvalue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearForm.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_uniform_when_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_uniform_when_equal","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L94-L121","doc":"If all δ_k have the same Frobenius norm, the weights are uniform:\nw_k = 1/N for all k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L75-L92","doc":"Each Gram weight is non-negative: w_k ≥ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_sum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight_sum_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L62-L73","doc":"The Gram weight is a probability distribution: Σ_k w_k = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramWeightedQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramWeightedQ","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L51-L60","doc":"The Gram-weighted Q-value:\nQ = (Σ_k w_k^G × Δ_k) × N × m_e ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramWeight","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L40-L49","doc":"The Gram weight for neutron k:\nw_k^G = ||δ_k||_F / Σ_j ||δ_j||_F ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nfReductionCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nfReductionCost","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L33-L38","doc":"The NF reduction cost Δ_k: change in L1 norm when neutron k converts.\nΔ_k = ||N_par||₁ - ||N_dau^(k)||₁ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusNorm","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L29-L31","doc":"The Frobenius norm: ||v||_F = √|v · G · v|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusNormSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusNormSq","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L24-L27","doc":"The Frobenius norm squared of a vector v with respect to Gram matrix G:\n||v||²_F = v · G · v = Σ_{ij} v_i G_{ij} v_j ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.entries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.entries","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GramMatrix","kind":"structure","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/gram-weighted-qvalue.lean#L17-L22","doc":"The Gram matrix G_{ij} = tr_M(b_i · b_j) of the Iwahori-Hecke\nalgebra restricted to a finite-dimensional NF subspace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}